<GuideLayout 
  title="Dropshipping vs. Wholesale: Which Model Fits Your Activewear Brand?" 
  type="BUSINESS MODEL"
  description="Compare the pros and cons of dropshipping and wholesale. Choose the distribution strategy that aligns with your capital and growth goals."
>
  <h2>Scaling Your Distribution</h2>
  <p>How you choose to deliver your products to the end consumer will dictate your profit margins, inventory risk, and brand control.</p>
  
  <h3>The Wholesale Model</h3>
  <p>In wholesale, you buy inventory in bulk (MOQ 100+) and store it in your own warehouse or a 3PL. 
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Pros:</strong> Higher profit margins, full control over packaging, and faster local shipping.</li>
      <li><strong>Cons:</strong> Requires upfront capital and carries inventory risk.</li>
    </ul>
  </p>

  <h3>The Dropshipping Model</h3>
  <p>You list products on your site, and the factory or supplier ships them directly to the customer when an order is placed.
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Pros:</strong> Low upfront cost and no inventory risk.</li>
      <li><strong>Cons:</strong> Lower margins, longer shipping times from China, and less control over the unboxing experience.</li>
    </ul>
  </p>

  <h3>The Hybrid Approach</h3>
  <p>Many successful Fitclo partners start with dropshipping to test designs and then move to a wholesale model for their best-selling "Hero" products to maximize profit and customer satisfaction.</p>
</GuideLayout>
